# The tools that make the AppImage (build_appimage.sh), pinned by release tag and
# by SHA-256: <file name> <url> <sha256, or PENDING>.
#
# PENDING means the hash has not been recorded yet: build_appimage.sh then
# downloads the file anyway, prints its hash and a warning, and carries on. That
# is trust on first use, and it is only until the author runs
#     src/platforms/linux/packaging/pin_linuxdeploy.sh
# on a machine they trust and commits the result; after that a download whose
# hash differs fails the build. Bump a tool by changing the tag in its url, setting
# the hash to PENDING and running the script again.
linuxdeploy-x86_64.AppImage https://github.com/linuxdeploy/linuxdeploy/releases/download/1-alpha-20251107-1/linuxdeploy-x86_64.AppImage PENDING
linuxdeploy-plugin-qt-x86_64.AppImage https://github.com/linuxdeploy/linuxdeploy-plugin-qt/releases/download/1-alpha-20250213-1/linuxdeploy-plugin-qt-x86_64.AppImage PENDING
